  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x26EE" flags="0x0">
    <title>Warm-up: end by speed, n_out/32 not below the byte, factory 48 = 1536 output rpm (0x70BAC). 0 = no warm-up program</title>
    <description>0x251A0 (the only reference) ends the warm-up program 0x25182 (19D0 pair 0x28D50; flag [0xFFFF9088], set at power-on). While it runs the shift matrices see the pedal [0xFFFF912C] = max(pedal, 0x7013A(engine temperature, program)). Other ends: bit 3 of CAN byte [0xFFFF83E1], the counter 0x71B52 or the table 0x7013A reaching 0. 19D0 pair 0x8B48. Document 05 called this a thermal derate until 06.10.2026: wrong, it is the warm-up.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="2" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x00" mmedaddress="0x70BAC" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>output shaft rpm / 32</units>
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
